# Fanatical Firebrand: its ability costs {T} (CR 602.2b), so a Firebrand tapped by attacking (no vigilance) cannot activate it. It
# attacks the turn it is cast thanks to haste and deals 1 combat damage; the refusal is judged in the combat damage step and the
# end of combat, with the Firebrand tapped. The control is the first Firebrand scenario, where the untapped Firebrand activates.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Fanatical Firebrand
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fanatical Firebrand.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Fanatical Firebrand > Bot2)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand.Activate
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand.Activate

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand.Tapped = true
